          "evidence": "The x-axis is labeled 'Year' and has ticks from 1880 to 1891.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "1. The horizontal axis binds the line's endpoints to years. 2. The vertical axis 'Number of Tourists' increases upward. 3. A later endpoint higher on the page represents a higher tourist count. 4. An overall increase across 1880-1891 maps to the 'growth-planning' option.",
        "evidence": "Condition 1 is supported by the x-axis ticks (1880-1891). Condition 2 is supported by the y-axis label and tick order. Condition 3 is supported by the visual geometry: the 1891 endpoint is higher than the 1880 start. Condition 4 is supported by the task options, where 'growth planning' corresponds to an increasing trend. All necessary conditions are established by the chart's visual encoding and the task's goal to match the 'overall visitor trend' shown in the dashboard.",
        "status": "supported"
      }
    }
  }
